.SH "DETAILS (client common)"
.PP
/app:command-pipe
.RS 4
Launches remote application programs by writing to a pipe\&.
.br

Launch format is JSON
.RE
.PP
Supported JSON object elements:
.RS 4
.PP
\fIflags\fR
.RS 4
.PP
.RS 4
\fIJSON integer\fR
.br

Mask of flags as documented in [MS-RDPERP] 2.2.2.3.1 Client Execute PDU (TS_RAIL_ORDER_EXEC)
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fIprogram\fR
.RS 4
.PP
.RS 4
\fIJSON string\fR
.br

The program to launch.
This option is required.
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fIworkingdir\fR
.RS 4
.PP
.RS 4
\fIJSON string\fR
.br

The working directory for the application to launch
.RE
.RE
.PP
\fIarguments\fR
.RS 4
.PP
\fIJSON string\fR
.RS 4
The arguments to pass to the application
.RE
.RE
.RE
.RE
.br

.PP
Example
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
echo '{"flags":1234,"program":"notepad","workingdir": "c:\\Users\\demo1\\Documents","arguments": "/PT file.txt printername printer.dll 1234"}' > $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/freerdp-rail-v1-<connection hash>.fifo
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}

